<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 190 0 R
/E (Karaoke is a form of entertainment in which people sing along to instrumental versions of songs while lyrics are displayed on a screen. However, karaoke is more than a music activity. It is also a participatory social experience because it involves performance, audience attention, turn-taking, and shared interaction in group settings. In the context of this project, karaoke is especially relevant because it often takes place in public or semi-public environments such as bars, karaoke rooms, parties, and organised social events, where users may experience confidence, embarrassment, self-presentation, and group participation at the same time \(Encyclopaedia Britannica, 2026\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
