297 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 192 0 R
/E (Contemporary karaoke is no longer confined to a single, standardised venue, but is now found across a wide variety of settings. In Japan, karaoke has evolved from a singing culture centred on bars into a broader service system, encompassing karaoke booths, bars, and other commercial venues such as hotels, coaches and restaurants. With the rise of the private karaoke booth model, a significant shift has taken place: private booths have made singing the primary purpose of a visit, rather than a secondary activity to drinking. This has also broadened participation, allowing users to interact in smaller, more intimate social settings. Consequently, contemporary karaoke can be understood not merely as a musical activity, but as a place-based social service shaped by space, privacy, technology and group interaction \(Green, 2022\).)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
