<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Contemporary karaoke increasingly depends on digital and connected interfaces rather than a single standalone machine. Mobile social karaoke systems can support group creation, song sharing, real-time messaging, and flexible participation through smartphones and cloud-based services, showing that karaoke technology shapes not only functional tasks but also social interaction and coordination \(Shin, 2023\). This creates clear opportunities for interface design to improve accessibility, emotional comfort, and inclusive participation across devices.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
